  <h1>MediaVault Web Clipper – Privacy Policy</h1>
  <small>Last updated: October 28, 2026</small>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    MediaVault Web Clipper is a browser extension that allows users to save
    selected web images to their locally running MediaVault desktop application.
  </p>

  <h2>Information Processed</h2>
  <p>
    When a user chooses to save an image, the extension may process the
    selected image URL, source page URL, page title, image alternative text,
    filename, and destination folder information. The information processed
    depends on the user's action and the information available on the page.
  </p>

  <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>
    This information is used to identify the selected image and fulfill the
    user's request to save it to MediaVault. Source page information may be
    saved alongside the item in the user's local library.
  </p>
  <p>
    The extension is not designed to build a browsing history, profile users,
    or deliver targeted advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Local Communication and Storage</h2>
  <p>
    The extension communicates with the MediaVault desktop application running
    on the user's computer through the local loopback address 127.0.0.1.
    This communication transfers information related to the image selected
    by the user.
  </p>
  <p>
    The extension does not operate a developer-controlled cloud service to
    collect or store this information. The MediaVault desktop application
    handles saved items according to its functionality and settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Website and Image Access</h2>
  <p>
    Website access supports the image-saving interface and user-selected
    images. The MediaVault application may request an image from its original
    host when saving it. Such requests are subject to the original host's
    policies and normal network behavior.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Sharing and Sale</h2>
  <p>
    The developer does not sell users' information. Information associated
    with a selected image is transferred to the user's local MediaVault
    application to provide the requested functionality. The extension is
    not designed to send this information to a developer-operated analytics
    or advertising service.
  </p>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>contextMenus:</strong> Adds an image context-menu action so
      users can initiate saving an image.</li>
    <li><strong>storage:</strong> Supports storage of extension state needed
      for its functionality.</li>
    <li><strong>activeTab:</strong> Supports user-initiated actions on the
      current tab.</li>
    <li><strong>Website access:</strong> Supports the in-page interface and
      processing of images selected by the user.</li>
    <li><strong>Localhost access:</strong> Enables communication with the
      MediaVault desktop application running on the user's computer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Remote Code</h2>
  <p>
    The extension's core functionality is implemented using code packaged
    with the extension. It does not download or execute remote JavaScript
    or WebAssembly code for its core functionality.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and Retention</h2>
  <p>
    The extension is designed to transfer clip information to the user's
    local application rather than a developer-operated cloud service.
    Users are responsible for securing their devices and local library data.
    Saved items can be managed according to the features available in
    MediaVault.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated if the extension's functionality or data
    practices change. The latest version will be published at this URL.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy-related questions, please use the
    <a href="https://github.com/mertkazancii/MediaVault/issues">
      MediaVault GitHub issue tracker
    </a>.
  </p>
</body>
